 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Numerical Underflow:** If `depth_sigma` is very small or depth differences are large, `exponent` can become very negative, causing `exp()` to underflow to zero. Clamping to `min_depth_exponent` prevents this [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Zero Total Weight:** If all weights are zero (e.g., due to aggressive clamping), division by zero occurs. A fallback to simple averaging or zero is required [G].
-*   **Boundary Conditions:** The calculation assumes `texcoord` falls within the valid range of the low-res texture. If the high-res fragment is near the edge of the screen, `texcoord` might point outside the low-res texture bounds. Standard texture sampling behavior (clamp, repeat, or border color) will apply, but this may introduce artifacts at the edges of the cloud volume [G].
