 ## Background
-Depth-aware upsampling for volumetric clouds was introduced by Jan Wedekind in the context of procedural volumetric cloud rendering [S1, unofficial]. It addresses the trade-off between visual quality (blue noise) and performance in real-time cloud rendering. The method builds on standard bilinear downsampling and upsampling techniques, adding a depth-aware weighting mechanism to preserve sharpness and reduce noise [S1, unofficial].
